DeepCW CW decoder — third-party components and provenance

- model.onnx, model.onnx.json: the DeepCW Morse-decoding model and its
  metadata from https://github.com/e04/deepcw-engine, licensed
  AGPL-3.0-only. The model files are NOT linked into the SDRg35xx
  binary; they are loaded at runtime by a separate sidecar process
  (same isolation pattern as the HamNoise and rtl_tcp sidecars), so
  the AGPL terms apply to that sidecar and its inputs/outputs, not to
  the main application.
- ONNX Runtime (libonnxruntime.so.*) from https://github.com/
  microsoft/onnxruntime, MIT License. Used only by the sidecar.
- tools/deepcw_bench.c: measurement harness written for this project;
  its spectrogram/CTC pipeline replicates the reference example in
  deepcw-engine/examples/python (AGPL-3.0-only) — kept as a standalone
  tool, not linked into the app.

Fetch instructions (binaries are gitignored, ~40 MB):
  model + metadata: raw.githubusercontent.com/e04/deepcw-engine/main/
  onnxruntime: github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime releases,
  onnxruntime-linux-aarch64-*.tgz (lib/libonnxruntime.so.1.* +
  lib/libonnxruntime_providers_shared.so + include/)

Streaming sidecar (tools/deepcw.c, tools/feeder.c): written for this
project; the spectrogram/CTC pipeline replicates the AGPL reference
example. tools/deepcw.c is the shipped sidecar source (built on-device
or cross-compiled, see tools/build_deepcw_on_device.sh); tools/feeder.c
is a test-only constant-rate file feeder.
